-- Sendzz on-chain activity: every USDC movement touching a Sendzz wallet, ONE ROW PER CHAIN
-- with each movement type as its own column.
--
-- Covers SIX EVM CHAINS **AND STELLAR** in one result, so the dashboard's activity chart shows
-- the whole product rather than a slice of it.
--
-- --- Why Stellar is unioned in here ------------------------------------------
--
-- It used to be a separate panel, and the chart on this query showed EVM only. A reviewer read
-- that chart, saw Base and nothing else, and took the Stellar settlement claim to be either a
-- submission error or a misleading one -- a fair reading of a chart that omits it.
--
-- The two rails are genuinely different underneath (an ERC-20 log versus a Stellar payment
-- operation, matched by two different address rosters), but that is an implementation detail.
-- From the product's side both are "USDC moved for a Sendzz user", so they belong on one axis.
-- Stellar keeps its own detail panel; this makes it visible in the headline.
--
-- --- Classification ----------------------------------------------------------
--
-- bridge_in   USDC minted here. CCTP mints from the zero address, or moves it out of one of
--             Circle's contracts. This is a bridge ARRIVING on this chain.
-- bridge_out  USDC burned here, which on-chain is a transfer to Circle's TokenMinterV2
--             (0xfd78EE91..., confirmed on BaseScan/Etherscan). A bridge LEAVING this chain.
-- deposit     Arrived from an address that is not ours. Users fund mostly from Binance and
--             Bybit.
-- transfer    Everything else leaving or moving between Sendzz wallets. Deliberately merges
--             user-to-user sends with sends to outside addresses -- they are the same action
--             from the product's side, and off-ramp payouts land here too.
-- fee         Sent to a Sendzz fee treasury. Classified so it is identifiable, then EXCLUDED
--             below: the dashboard is about user money, not our revenue.
--
-- Stellar contributes `deposit` and `transfer` only. Its bridges are Soroban contract calls,
-- not payment operations, so they are invisible to this query by construction -- read the
-- bridge_movements note in dune/README.md before comparing bridge legs across rails.
--
-- --- Coverage ----------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- EVM:     either side of the transfer is a Sendzz address.
-- Stellar: our gas station paid the fee, OR either side is a Sendzz address. The second half is
--          not optional -- an inbound deposit is paid for by the SENDER, so a gas-station-only
--          filter hid 80 payments worth 12,502.79 USDC, more than it reported.
--
-- --- Performance -------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Addresses are inline, not joined from the roster: joining costs ~96s against Dune's 120s
-- ceiling and the EVM half alone runs in ~45s. REGENERATE both lists when new users sign up, or
-- their volume goes silently missing. Both halves are date- and chain-bounded; without that
-- neither finishes.
--
-- avalanche_c is Dune's name for Avalanche C-Chain -- confirmed, not guessed.
--
-- --- Arc, and why it may read as zero -----------------------------------------
--
-- Arc is in the chain list, and the roster needs nothing added: a Circle smart account is
-- CREATE2-deterministic, so a user's address on Arc is the same one already listed here.
--
-- Two reasons it can still show nothing, neither of which is a bug in this query:
--
--   1. Dune may not index Arc yet. It launched 2026-09-16. An unindexed chain returns no rows
--      rather than erroring, so this is silent -- check for `arc` in the output before quoting
--      any Arc figure.
--   2. USDC is Arc's NATIVE GAS TOKEN as well as a precompile at 0x3600...0000. An ordinary
--      wallet-to-wallet send there is a native transfer, NOT an ERC-20 Transfer event, and
--      `tokens.transfers` is built from ERC-20 logs. So this query may capture CCTP mints and
--      precompile transfers while missing ordinary sends entirely.
--
-- The app hit exactly this: the deposit scanner queried erc20 logs only and a real 0.5 USDC
-- deposit was invisible while the balance moved -- see transferCategories in
-- lib/web3/deposit-scanner.ts. If Arc volume looks low against the app's own numbers, that
-- asymmetry is the first thing to check, not the roster.

WITH evm AS (
  SELECT
    tr.blockchain             AS chain,
    CAST(tr.amount AS double) AS usdc,
    CASE
      WHEN tr."from" = 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
        OR tr."from" IN (0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002,
                         0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d,
                         0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64) THEN 'bridge_in'
      WHEN tr."to"   = 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
        OR tr."to"   IN (0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002,
                         0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d,
                         0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64) THEN 'bridge_out'
      WHEN tr."to"   IN (0x177ce46b514aDe0f552D1C2c54f5De9256CD99b9,
                         0x432bf05E6E63a7e24340AD36148E1a9BCe7A99c2) THEN 'fee'
      WHEN tr."to" IN (0x13bd0512365d12cd624be0dc1ffe753eb0d15c94, 0x9f90ae09197d5699a103595d6346d1a25775a613, 0x782edfa8fbfb075f500cd01a8f211815fd0998de, 0xe1d52fe2fa4e2d158d8e08eaebf938ad4b6e973c, 0x2b472d9d43887c447a793dfc78ded96a1e9b7899, 0xe9f22286a19ef6a0d8a73328f0494035b4bf05c9, 0x598ce4ac34cad18e0b0d58735ba1be0c4ccb5329, 0xee8100b30684aec3b793da0884fbcaa256e96dd9, 0xf4d2095155d5370b537bdd697587d9eaa6fcada4, 0xf4d2095155d5370b537bdd697587d9eaa6fcada4, 0xbc015b8d7a860400621b2bc1bd8f062614e5998a, 0xb5842e4549406154e17a952a0911f7ee08cb085b, 0x04056ff0be4d2cc641f365b98f2e9578f072fd1e, 0x3941a067d68f386dc76f81d26f76a6053ff0790a, 0x0d90f53bf00c18e3fac732eb151740fe596f5457, 0x89e3c3b03f3a6b138c6b08a7eb58c8945fb2d633, 0x8658bd8576ffc1d827c927f858af056a47e564fa, 0x8658bd8576ffc1d827c927f858af056a47e564fa, 0xd9efdfcfe7cc6b4f988d1af7e833bd5a60d6ee02, 0xb86e4d9bdce86d94c479b4ce4794152aed3d93ce, 0x8e2497dfc9e7dad595ad214da8ace0d69ac632ca, 0xecc82920b2bf64c85573ab1af57641c5418597e8, 0xecc82920b2bf64c85573ab1af57641c5418597e8, 0x3f62f83b10ff5abce4f3304e3f482a1691df4aab, 0xcd62b0963b554d354c670b33a2ecdfac4472bd53, 0xd8854db2d3793693d4d9a15d8037e59458caadd9, 0x376e3a544906d9686867b94eee5371b1811325f4, 0x5d83f02c82c387d6b8025aa484792fb74a4fea8e, 0x0e1e57c650725ff6edf87e3f595b5aad79f6b411, 0x06e2361e360be2fb64686e8c8cd22046821efdac, 0xbf8377bb2e8e52202f758c6cc2122dd0ab7119fa, 0x8b9742f6370cc6fc293f059de7777e93085a6401, 0xf2af457ce168175643d83c080b8aa9005f9f39b1, 0xb1ba64056a274c7372d34fcaaf17240a9a3ce3b8, 0x2bba27c3c984f51d6017cbe11ece1707e95177d6, 0x44809b5b1d2d35cf9d22e89557183e4444b9a5f6, 0x37ba366826a37abdcac8140949c4c8dc606e98a9, 0x5d8695c69167d248e6a530db17732f45fa686f2e, 0x889e82c4b6ca2c1ecfc309a8e77033ebf33d44d3, 0xfe5f6d90b8078fde5a0ef93a9115cb4ef6869c9a, 0xcbaed99c636dbe8fe4d9ac01a8d27d64ce486f49, 0xe125c6d7f8463ae22a7ede1efa48adb1ee23ccac, 0x05ab1807627dc87d3688f52544cb633fca0ead1f, 0x224fd1ced2449976a5f2ec71425b49f1b72c0ab2, 0x8a16aecb6eebce96dbc6fb2010110e28aff0e0f